if they have longer careers,

00:13:48.662 --> 00:13:50.680
they patent much more,

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.200
they patent higher quality innovations,

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.750
but there's of course
something special about them.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.650
What I think is our main

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.140
and most important result is this one.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:06.090
And it's that GMIs are
significantly more present

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.270
in the first stages of the development

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:11.373
of a new technology class in
their countries of destination.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.957
And I'm going to show you a
little bit of evidence of this.

00:14:14.957 --> 00:14:17.140
And it goes back a
little bit to the example

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.123
of the beginning of Ismael Mena.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:24.790
We also find that this
prevalence disappears over time.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:28.623
So like, as the life cycle
of a technology advances,

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.640
we see less presence of GMIs,

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:36.290
which dwarfs, could be
interpreted as a sign that once,

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.883
once that knowledge has been transferred,

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:42.450
as more and more patents
are being invented

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:43.620
in that technology,

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:46.760
the knowledge becomes embedded
in the local inventors.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.270
And once I get to their craft,

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:50.720
I'm gonna be more specific
about what I'm saying.

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:56.250
We don't find strong evidence
though, that the quality

00:14:56.250 --> 00:15:01.250
